Subject: layouts/us: more letters under a long press

A long press on a letter offers its accented forms. The US layout had a
handful; this adds the ones names and loanwords need most (ě ẽ ė ę, ÿ, į,
ś š, ł and the like), each letter's commonest forms nearest the finger.
